#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:3
#: b8361e0d40e5427595ac968ebcbd7ca8
msgid "Dom0 secure updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:7
#: 6f50e3bb56424fe8838b86072ede3412
msgid "Reasons for Dom0 updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:10
#: 9578ff2e23014216873e92724d95a1dd
msgid ""
"Normally there should be few reasons for updating software in Dom0. This is "
"because there is no networking in Dom0, which means that even if some bugs "
"will be discovered e.g. in the Dom0 Desktop Manager, this really is not a "
"problem for Qubes, because all the third-party software running in Dom0 is "
"not accessible from VMs or network in any way. Some exceptions to the above "
"include: Qubes GUI daemon, Xen store daemon, and disk back-ends (we plan to "
"move the disk backends to untrusted domain in Qubes 2.0). Of course we "
"believe this software is reasonably secure and we hope it will not need "
"patching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:12
#: 610e5c3457854e1882f10f74d22665c8
msgid ""
"However, we anticipate some other situations when updating Dom0 software "
"might be required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:14
#: 47e7b9fcfc4147f1b2ca7cb3f2c1f22a
msgid "Updating drivers/libs for new hardware support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:16
#: 9bbd036c1ad24c03bd114ab270ef30a9
msgid ""
"Correcting non-security related bugs (e.g. new buttons for qubes manager)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:18
#: 5b60bece8def46c783976eba4eaf0047
msgid "Adding new features (e.g. GUI backup tool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:23
#: f042fb89de1e4b1aa7b30ce813f3dcd1
msgid "Problems with traditional network-based update mechanisms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:26
#: 57602437a6ae488faf9c56cd5a19811c
msgid ""
"Dom0 is the most trusted domain on Qubes OS, and for this reason we decided "
"to design Qubes in such a way that Dom0 is not connected to any network. In "
"fact only certain domains can be connected to a network via so-called "
"network domains. There can also be more than one network domain, e.g. in "
"case the user is connected to more than one physically or logically "
"separated networks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:29
#: 843b5085c53d4f41bbafa39df015a865
msgid "Secure update mechanism we use in Qubes (starting from Beta 2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:32
#: 9a88f81ac1bb4550a745cbe188761385
msgid ""
"Keeping Dom0 not connected to any network makes it hard, however, to provide "
"updates for software in Dom0. For this reason we have come up with the "
"following mechanism for Dom0 updates, which minimizes the amount of "
"untrusted input processed by Dom0 software:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:34
#: fa9c1f3fa1f742b9b499e241f7090aad
msgid ""
"The update process is initiated by `qubes-dom0-update script <https://github."
"com/QubesOS/qubes-core-admin-linux/blob/release2/dom0-updates/qubes-dom0-"
"update>`__, running in Dom0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:36
#: a95c60db2d7e453f88444659749906e9
msgid ""
"Updates (``*.rpm`` files) are checked and downloaded by UpdateVM, which by "
"default is the same as the firewall VM, but can be configured to be any "
"other, network-connected VM. This is done by `qubes-download-dom0-updates.sh "
"script <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-core-agent-linux/blob/release2/misc/"
"qubes-download-dom0-updates.sh>`__ (this script is executed using qrexec by "
"the previously mentioned qubes-dom0-update). Note that we assume that this "
"script might get compromised and fetch maliciously compromised downloads – "
"this is not a problem as Dom0 verifies digital signatures on updates later. "
"The downloaded rpm files are placed in a ``/var/lib/qubes/dom0-updates`` "
"directory on UpdateVM filesystem (again, they might get compromised while "
"being kept there, still this isn’t a problem). This directory is passed to "
"yum using the ``--installroot=`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:38
#: f8eabb8453174ba2a7a775dcace08482
msgid ""
"Once updates are downloaded, the update script that runs in UpdateVM "
"requests an RPM service `qubes.ReceiveUpdates <https://github.com/QubesOS/"
"qubes-core-admin-linux/blob/release2/dom0-updates/qubes.ReceiveUpdates>`__ "
"to be executed in Dom0. This service is implemented by `qubes-receive-"
"updates script <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-core-admin-linux/blob/"
"release2/dom0-updates/qubes-receive-updates>`__ running in Dom0. The Dom0’s "
"qubes-dom0-update script (which originally initiated the whole update "
"process) waits until qubes-receive-updates finished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:40
#: 3702dc734c624176b5a8e766049c1e14
msgid ""
"The qubes-receive-updates script processes the untrusted input from Update "
"VM: it first extracts the received ``*.rpm`` files (that are sent over "
"qrexec data connection) and then verifies digital signature on each file. "
"The qubes-receive-updates script is a security-critical component of the "
"Dom0 update process (as is the `qfile-dom0-unpacker.c <https://github.com/"
"QubesOS/qubes-core-admin-linux/blob/release2/dom0-updates/qfile-dom0-"
"unpacker.c>`__ and the rpm utility, both used by the qubes-receive-updates "
"for processing the untrusted input)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:42
#: d538fd78e5e04364a498a26c7f5dc883
msgid ""
"Once qubes-receive-updates finished unpacking and verifying the updates, the "
"updates are placed in ``qubes-receive-updates`` directory in Dom0 "
"filesystem. Those updates are now trusted. Dom0 is configured (see /etc/yum."
"conf in Dom0) to use this directory as a default (and only) `yum repository "
"<https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-core-admin-linux/blob/release2/dom0-"
"updates/qubes-cached.repo>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:44
#: 76e4b7ec9aef416ead98bd2bb21380b3
msgid ""
"Finally, qubes-dom0-update runs ``yum update`` that fetches the RPMs from "
"qubes-cached repo and installs them as usual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:47
#: 6d896eac80324bf5a6dfe206642e892f
msgid "Security benefit of our update mechanism"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/dom0-secure-updates.rst:50
#: b084319eabf94d71969b6cad0ce0fdb2
msgid ""
"The benefit of the above scheme is that one doesn’t need to trust the TCP/IP "
"stack, the HTTP stack, and wget implementation in order to safely deliver "
"and install updates in Dom0. One only needs to trust a few hundred lines of "
"code as discussed above, as well as the rpm utility for properly checking "
"digital signature (but this is required in any update scheme)."
msgstr ""
